<title>USA: U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to watch - Nov 27.</title>
<headline>U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to watch - Nov 27.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>* Virgin Express, Richard Branson's new no-frills airline, is in talks with Boeing Co about buying 25 737-700 jets worth as much as $1.1 billion, The Wall Street Journal reported. Boeing's stock closed at 99-1/4.</p>
<p>* Primark Corp will announce on Wednesday it has bought Baseline Financial Services for $40 million from Bowne &amp; Co Inc and Robert Patterson, Baseline's founder, the New York Times reported. Primark closed at 26 and Bowne closed at 24.</p>
